# Livetext User Documentation

Livetext transforms plain text to HTML with powerful formatting, variables, functions, and extensibility.

## Installation

gem install livetext

## Basic Text Formatting

Livetext uses simple markers for text formatting:

*This is bold text
_This is italic text
`This is code
~This is strikethrough

You can combine them: *bold _italic text

Note: The markers are processed and converted to HTML tags.

## Variables

Variables store data and are referenced with \$variable. Predefined variables are always capitalized:

- \$File - current file being processed
- \$View - current view or context

Set variables with the .set command:

.set name=John
.set count=42

Reference them: Hello $name, you have $count items.

## Dot Commands

Dot commands start with \. and control document processing:

### Basic Commands
.h1 Main Title
.h2 Section Title
.br
.set variable=value

### Function Definition
.func myfunction
  return "Hello, World!"
.end

### Mixins and Imports
.mixin tutorial

## Functions

Functions are called with \$\$function syntax.

### Built-in Functions
$$date - current date
$$time - current time
$$pwd - current directory

### User-defined Functions
Create functions with .func:

.func greet
  return "Hello, $name!"
.end

Call them: $$greet

## Advanced Features

### Custom Dot Commands
Create reusable functionality with mixins:

.mixin tutorial

Create a mixin file plugin/mytools.rb:

def sort_list(args, data)
  items = data.split("\n").sort
  items.join("\n")
end

### Variable Access in Functions
Functions can access variables through the Livetext instance:

class Livetext::Functions
  def get_user_info(param)
    user = @live.vars.User || "unknown"
    "User: #{user}"
  end
end

## Examples

### Simple Documentation
.h1 API Reference
.set version=1.2.3

This is version $version of the API.

.func format_code
  return "<pre><code>#{param}</code></pre>"
.end

$$format_code:function example() { return true; }

### Data Table
.set items=apple,banana,cherry

.h2 Fruit List
.func list_items
  items = param.split(",")
  html = "<ul>"
  items.each { |item| html += "<li>#{item}</li>" }
  html += "</ul>"
  return html
.end

$$list_items:$items

## Use Cases and Ideas

### Ad Hoc Solutions
- **Sorted Lists**: Create a .sort command that sorts list items alphabetically
- **Date Formatting**: Custom date functions for different locales
- **Data Processing**: Transform CSV data into formatted tables

### Plugin Possibilities
- **PDF Generation**: Convert Livetext to PDF
- **SVG Graphics**: Generate charts and diagrams
- **Image Processing**: Integrate with RMagick for image manipulation
- **Database Integration**: Pull data from databases
- **API Integration**: Fetch data from web services

## File Extensions

- .lt3 - Livetext source files
- .rb - Ruby mixin/plugin files

## Getting Help

Use .debug to see what Livetext is processing:

.debug
This will show debug output
.end
